WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.240
House of the Dragon is coming in less than
a year.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:09.349
Set 168 years before Game of Thrones, this,
Targaryen based prequel show, which focuses

00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:12.690
on the Targaryen civil war known as the Dance
of the Dragons,

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.840
will obviously have many similarities with
Game of Thrones, one of which is Valyrian

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.600
steel swords.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.660
Valyrian steel is a form of metal that was
forged in the days of the mighty Valyrian

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.119
Freehold.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:30.810
When fashioned into bladed weapons, the steel
can hold an especially keen edge, remaining

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.570
sharp forever without the need for honing.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.720
It’s confirmed that House of the Dragon
will feature 3 Valyrian swords in season 1

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.809
with a few joining later on in the show.

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:47.780
Invented in Targaryen’s original home, Valyria,
these swords are of unparalleled quality.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.649
George RR Martin says that if the two fighters
of equal skill and power met on the field,

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:56.160
the one with Valyrian steel in his hands will
win.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.890
That’s how much of a change it makes.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.570
Almost all of the legendary warriors of Westeros
have wielded it.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:07.350
What makes Valyrian steel swords so unique
is that it’s extremely rare and its blades

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.110
are lighter, stronger, and sharper in comparison
to ordinary steel.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:17.250
Valyrian steel, possibly formed with dragons
and definitely forged with magic and spells,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.820
was manufactured in the Valyrian Freehold
of old.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:26.020
According to legend, Valyrian steel was made
with dragon-fire and infused with magical

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:32.780
spells - some say with blood magic, literally
requiring "fire and blood" (like House Targaryen’s

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.780
motto).

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.050
After the Doom of Valyria, just as all the
Valyrians and their dragons (except Targaryens

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:44.360
and their dragons), all was destroyed, including
the secret of making the Valyrian steel.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.740
Valyrian steel was always costly, but it became
considerably more so when there was no more

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.680
Valyria, the secret of its making lost with
the Doom.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.020
Only the greatest weaponsmiths can reforge
swords from existing Valyrian steel, making

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.329
those remaining weapons highly treasured and
extremely rare.

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:06.909
However, there are still plenty of them in
Westeros and especially in this time period

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:12.110
of the Targaryen civil war, which includes
the two that Targaryens owned which we never

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.980
had the opportunity to see in Game of Thrones
as they got lost in meantime.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:21.640
So let’s see which 3 Valyrian swords will
House of the Dragon feature in season 1 and

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.890
which will join in the later seasons.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:29.239
Targaryen’s Blackfyre and Dark Sister along
with Stark’s Ice are the 3 Valyrian steel

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:31.220
swords we’ll see in season 1.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:36.170
Orphan-Maker, Lamentation, Vigilance, and
Lady Forlorn are the names of the remaining

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.330
Valyrian swords that will appear by the end
of the series.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.530
Let’s start with the most famous of them
all and possibly the most legendary of them

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.550
all, House Targaryen’s Blackfyre.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:53.150
Blackfyre is a Valyrian steel sword that originally
belonged to Aegon I Targaryen, Blackfyre is

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:58.849
a fabled hand-and-a-half longsword of Valyrian
steel once wielded by Aegon the Conqueror

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:01.780
during the Targaryen Conquest of the Seven
Kingdoms.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.409
Afterward, it became the treasured ancestral
blade of House Targaryen, carried by kings

00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:09.080
and princes.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.599
During the story of House of the Dragon, and
therefore during the Targaryen civil war,

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:15.659
it belonged to Aegon II.

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:21.720
Aegon II Targaryen's possession of Blackfyre
enhanced his legitimacy against his rival,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.959
Rhaenyra Targaryen, during the Dance of the
Dragons.

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:24.959
When Aegon returned to King's Landing near
the end of the Targaryen civil war, he allowed

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:25.959
the condemned Trystane Truefyre to be granted
knighthood before his death.

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:26.959
Ser Marston Waters dubbed the youth Ser Trystane
Fyre, and Ser Alfred Broome then beheaded

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:27.959
the newly-made knight with Blackfyre.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:30.080
Before and after this, Blackfyre was wielded
by many great warriors and no doubt seeing

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.260
such a legendary sword will be amazing.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:38.489
Coming as the second Valyrian sword we’ll
see in season 1 is also from House Targaryen

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:41.600
and as you’ve probably guessed it by now,
it’s Dark Sister.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.040
The Dark Sister is the name of the famous
longsword of Valyrian steel once belonging

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.170
to Visenya Targaryen, the sister-wife of Aegon
the Conqueror.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:55.380
A great warrior, she used it in battle as
well as riding her dragon during the War of

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.549
Conquest.

00:03:56.549 --> 00:04:02.270
In our story, it’s used by another legendary
warrior Prince named Daemon Targaryen.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:07.430
Prince Daemon Targaryen was given Dark Sister
by King Jaehaerys I for his prowess.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:13.379
Ser Criston Cole defeated Daemon in a tourney
for King Viserys I's accession, knocking Dark

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:16.810
Sister from the prince's hand with a morning
Star.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:22.080
Daemon wields Dark Sister during his war for
the Stepstones.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.880
In 115 AC, he defeats the Braavosi betrothed
of Laena Velaryon with the blade in a duel.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.940
During the Dance of the Dragons, and during
one of the most epic fights in Westerosi history,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.490
Daemon fights against Aemond Targaryen with
the blade in the Battle Above the Gods Eye,

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:43.630
leaping from the back of his dragon, Caraxes,
to plunge Dark Sister into Aemond's eye.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.861
When Aemond's bones were found some years
later in the waters of the Gods Eye, Dark

00:04:48.861 --> 00:04:52.919
Sister was still thrust hilt-deep through
his eye socket.

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:57.711
Cannot help but think of this Daemon’s statement
that’s written in Fire And Blood book: Dark

00:04:57.711 --> 00:05:01.800
Sister was made for nobler tasks than slaughtering
sheep.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.250
She has a thirst for blood.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:06.030
—Daemon Targaryen to Corlys Velaryon.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.690
The Third and final Valyrian steel sword we’ll
see in season 1 of House of the Dragon is

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:12.990
the one you’ve already seen in Game of Thrones.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:16.710
It’s House Stark’s ancestral greatsword
Ice.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:23.260
It’s as wide across as a man's hand and
six feet long and taller even than Robb Stark.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:28.669
The blade is Valyrian steel, spell-forged
and dark as smoke with deep rippling.

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:34.539
The name "Ice" is a legacy from the Age of
Heroes and predates the current sword.

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:39.979
About four hundred years before King Robert
I Baratheon's reign, the Valyrian steel greatsword

00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:46.710
was spell-forged in Valyria and acquired by
House Stark, who named it after that legacy.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:51.530
During House of the Dragon, it’s wielded
by legendary Cregan Stark who supports Rhaenyra

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:55.919
Targaryen and marches south to support her
claim.

00:05:55.919 --> 00:06:00.960
Lord Cregan Stark will use Ice to behead all
the traitors when he arrives in King's Landing,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.680
time in the capital which became known as
the Hour of the Wolf.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.690
Lord Stark will also use it in his fight against
Aemon the Dragonknight who is said to be House

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:15.700
Targaryen’s finest warrior and about whom
you can still hear songs all over Westeros.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:21.210
Those are the 3 we will see in season 1, but
later seasons will feature many more of them.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:26.690
One of them is Lamentation, a famed Valyrian
steel sword that belongs to House Royce.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:30.729
Ser Willam Royce wields the blade during the
Dance of the Dragons.

00:06:30.729 --> 00:06:34.889
The sword is torn from the hand of Willam,
however, when he is killed during the Ride

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.440
of the Seven.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.759
With Willam's death, the sword is carried
off, never to be found again.

00:06:40.759 --> 00:06:46.979
However, some rumors claim that Ser Warrick
Wheaton slashed a wing off of Syrax with a

00:06:46.979 --> 00:06:51.950
Valyrian steel sword, likely Lamentation,
during the Storming of the Dragonpit.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:55.169
Next sword that will appear later on is Vigilance.

00:06:55.169 --> 00:06:58.810
This Valyrian steel longsword belongs to House
Hightower.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:03.160
Lord Ormund Hightower wields the blade during
the Targaryen civil war fighting for king

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.980
Aegon II.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.590
After the Battle on the Honeywine, he used
it to knight his squire, the king's brother,

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:14.840
Prince Daeron dubbing him "Ser Daeron the
Daring", for turning the battle in his favor

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.280
with his dragon Tessarion.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.190
Lord Ormund is killed by Roddy the Ruin, leader
of Stark’s elite army Winter Wolves at the

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.360
Battle of Tumbleton.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:28.070
It’s unknown what happened to Vigilance
afterward.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:33.630
Another sword we’ll see later on is Orphan-Maker,
a Valyrian steel longsword with a black blade

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.960
belonging to House Roxton.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.781
Ser Jon Roxton wields the blade during the
Dance of the Dragons while fighting for King

00:07:40.781 --> 00:07:43.819
Aegon II Targaryen and the greens.

00:07:43.819 --> 00:07:50.419
During the Battle on the Honeywine, he used
it to deliver a fatal wound to Lord Owen Costayne.

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:55.780
During the Second Battle of Tumbleton, Jon
slew Hugh Hammer with Orphan-Maker, splitting

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.919
him from groin to throat.

00:07:57.919 --> 00:08:02.810
Shortly thereafter he was killed by Hugh's
men in a ten against one fight.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:06.560
The sword came into possession of Lord Unwin
Peake.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.690
When Peake became Hand of the King during
the regency of young king Aegon III Targaryen

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:18.590
in 133 AC, he drew Orphan-Maker, declaring
that, unlike the previous Hand, the blind

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:22.960
and crippled Ser Tyland Lannister, he could
still wield a sword.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.759
The sword's current whereabouts are unknown.

00:08:25.759 --> 00:08:30.330
The final and one of the most legendary Valyrian
steel swords in Westeros that we’ll see

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.479
is Lady Forlorn.

00:08:31.479 --> 00:08:35.570
It’s the ancestral longsword of House Corbray.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:41.120
Lady Forlorn is traditionally passed down
from lord to lord, but examples of lords lending

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:46.200
the blade to a son or a brother for their
lifetime only to have it return to the lord

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.920
afterward have been recorded in the history
of the house.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.100
Lady Forlorn has a heart-shaped ruby in its
pommel.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.230
Its Valyrian steel is smoke-grey in appearance.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:02.890
The name "Lady Forlorn" is a legacy from the
coming of the Andals, and predates the current

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:03.890
sword.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:09.880
Robar II Royce, the High King of the First
Men of the Vale, claimed the first Lady Forlorn

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:15.410
after slaying Qyle Corbray, the King of the
Fingers and the Andal leader.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:21.240
Robar wielded Lady Forlorn during the Battle
of the Seven Stars, using it to kill Torgold

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:25.240
Tollett and a decoy dressed as Ser Artys Arryn.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:30.230
The Corbrays claim that Ser Jaime Corbray
slew Robar in the battle, allowing them to

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:33.050
reclaim the first Lady Forlorn.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.640
At some point, the Corbrays acquired a Valyrian
steel sword which they named Lady Forlorn

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.779
in honor of the ancient sword.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:46.529
Ser Corwyn Corbray, the brother of Lord Leowyn
Corbray, wields Lady Forlorn during the Dance

00:09:46.529 --> 00:09:47.769
of the Dragons.

00:09:47.769 --> 00:09:53.399
Corwyn, one of the regents for Aegon III,
is slain by a crossbowman at Runestone after

00:09:53.399 --> 00:09:57.080
drawing Lady Forlorn on Lord Gunthor Royce.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.070
Those are all the Valyrian steel swords that
we’ll see in the House of the Dragon.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:06.220
The most legendary of them: Ice, Blackfyre,
and Dark Sister you’ll see in season 1 with

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:09.160
others coming and going throughout the series.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.649
The Game of Thrones prequel series, House
of the Dragon, based on the book Fire And

00:10:12.649 --> 00:10:15.580
Blood will air in 2022 on HBO.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:16.820
Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.370
If you enjoyed this video please give it a
big thumbs up and I hope to see you in the

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:26.269
next one, peace!

